  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AGD Pacific Legal Policy Twinning Program 2022-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Attorney-General&apos;s Department hosted 15 law and justice officials and police officers from a number of Pacific island countries as part of the Pacific Legal Policy Champions Program. Over a 2 week period participants were trained to deliver AGD&apos;s Legal Policy Development Course, so they can then deliver the course to other officers in their countries, &amp; various experts &amp; government stakeholders spoke to the officers on policy issues and topics to supplement learnings in the course. As a part of this, 1 of AGS&apos;s lawyers provided 1.5 days of pro bono in April 2023 training in relation to presentation &amp; facilitation skills. AGD worked with 2 officers who stayed for a further 6 weeks on priority law reform projects for their countries under the Twinning Program. The 2 projects were proposed reforms to Solomon Islands&apos; Evidence Act to provide for the special arrangement of allowing vulnerable witnesses to give their evidence via audio-visual recording and bail law reforms for Kiribati.</narrative>
  </description>
